  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The hash algorithms HAVAL, TIGER and WHIRLPOOL are currently not supported by Fedora although the documentation suggests otherwise. Out of the box JDK6 provides support for MD2, MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512. Other algorithms can be supported by plugging in a provider, like jacksum[1] as described here[2].",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The alternative course of action would be to remove these checksum algorithms from the documentation and the code in fedora/server/storage/types/Datastream.java",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "[1] ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.jonelo.de/java/jacksum/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.jonelo.de/java/jacksum/",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "[2] ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://java.sun.com/javase/6/docs/technotes/guides/security/crypto/CryptoSpec.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://java.sun.com/javase/6/docs/technotes/guides/security/crypto/CryptoSpec.html",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
