  "description": "<p>The hash algorithms HAVAL, TIGER and WHIRLPOOL are currently not supported by Fedora although the documentation suggests otherwise. Out of the box JDK6 provides support for MD2, MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512. Other algorithms can be supported by plugging in a provider, like jacksum<span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> as described here<span class=\"error\">&#91;2&#93;</span>.</p>\n\n<p>The alternative course of action would be to remove these checksum algorithms from the documentation and the code in fedora/server/storage/types/Datastream.java</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> <a href=\"http://www.jonelo.de/java/jacksum/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.jonelo.de/java/jacksum/</a><br/>\n<span class=\"error\">&#91;2&#93;</span> <a href=\"http://java.sun.com/javase/6/docs/technotes/guides/security/crypto/CryptoSpec.html\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://java.sun.com/javase/6/docs/technotes/guides/security/crypto/CryptoSpec.html</a></p>",
